WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.138
You linted the program's six workflow
files and three broken ones.

3
00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.725
You planned a create and a new
version against a tenant export,

4
00:00:08.725 --> 00:00:10.976
and saw a portal-made workflow flagged.

5
00:00:10.976 --> 00:00:14.550
And you measured a day-one readiness
rate of twenty-five percent.

6
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:19.339
Carry one thing forward: the day-one
workflow requests the onboarding package,

7
00:00:19.339 --> 00:00:22.212
but department access
comes from the next gate.

8
00:00:22.212 --> 00:00:27.637
Next is Module 4: assign access from
attributes and review what a move leaves.

9
00:00:27.637 --> 00:00:31.942
You'll lint access package assignment
policies before they reach the tenant,

10
00:00:31.942 --> 00:00:34.902
scan the tenant's policies
for the member-of operator,

11
00:00:34.902 --> 00:00:38.810
and list what a move leaves behind
for the manager of record to review.
